<title>GREECE: Greek June core CPI inflation drops to 7.0pct y/y.</title>
<headline>Greek June core CPI inflation drops to 7.0pct y/y.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-06-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greece's core CPI inflation which does not include volatile food and energy prices fell to 7.0 percent year-on-year in June from 7.6 percent in May, a central bank official told Reuters.</p>
<p>The Bank of Greece uses the OECD definition in calculating underlying inflation.</p>
<p>Headline inflation firmed to 5.5 percent year-on-year in June from 5.4 percent in May.</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
